      "side": 1,
      "message": "Previously, even if clcb was freed, such pointers would point to a valid piece of memory that was not in_use.\nLifecycle of tGATT_CMD_Q that holds tGATT_CMD_Q is not tied to p_clcb.\nNow it would be a dangling pointer causing crashes.\nHow do you ensure accessing freed pointer never happens ?\nShouldn\u0027t shared pointer be used for such things ?",
